### Summary of Design Decisions

| Milestone | Rule Type | Rationale |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|
| find spruce_door | `position_near_with_facing` (dist≤5, facing≤60°) | Preferred for find/locate tasks; models "player sees the door" |
| close door | `position_near_with_facing` (dist≤2, facing≤60°) + `count_in_box_at_least` | Tight proximity confirms interaction range; block existence check confirms door wasn't destroyed. Block state (open/closed) cannot be verified with available rules — this is an acknowledged limitation. |

### Acknowledged Limitation
The "close door" milestone cannot verify the actual closed state of the door. It verifies the **preconditions** for closing (player at interaction range, facing door, door exists) but not the **outcome**. This is the best achievable verification given the available rule types, which don't support block property/state checks.
